vulkan-game: two source files

Only client.cpp and server.cpp are compiled as game application sources.
The source content is an inlined amalgamation of the original full-feature
implementation at main e21c3a280e: rendering, editor, asset import,
animation, networking, movement, weapon logic, and server authority.
Shaders and original game assets remain separate data files.

The renderer uses VulkanWrapper and VulkanSystems modules. Other external
dependencies are still required for original behavior: GLFW (window/input),
fastgltf (GLB import), Ozz (rigs/animation), stb (image decode), and
Mbed TLS (DTLS). Those are preserved by build.c; removing them requires
replacement implementations and is not part of this amalgamation.

Build:
  git submodule update --init --recursive
  c build vulkan-server
  c build vulkan-client

Run:
  c build run vulkan-server
  c build run vulkan-client

IMPORTANT: The full native build and runtime visual/feature parity have not
yet been verified in a Vulkan/MoltenVK environment. Do not treat source-level
amalgamation alone as a validated engine rewrite.
